h1. SCORM Player Accessibility Issues: Missing Page Title and Iframe Title Attributes

h2. Summary

The SCORM player in Moodle has two critical accessibility violations:

# Missing page title when SCORM opens in popup mode
# Missing title attribute on the SCORM content iframe

These violations fail WCAG 2.1 Level A requirements and prevent screen reader users from understanding the page context.

h2. Environment

* Moodle version: 4.5 (and earlier versions)
* Affected component: mod/scorm
* Browser: All browsers
* Screen readers affected: JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver, etc.

h2. Issue 1: Missing Page Title in Popup Mode

h3. Description

When a SCORM activity opens in popup mode ({{$displaymode == 'popup'}}), the page title is not set, resulting in an empty {{<title></title>}} element in the HTML head.

h3. Steps to Reproduce

# Create a SCORM activity with "Display in new window" option enabled
# Launch the SCORM activity
# Inspect the popup window's HTML or check the browser tab
# Observe that the {{<title>}} element is empty

h3. Expected Result

The popup window should have a meaningful title, such as the SCORM activity name.

h3. Actual Result

The {{<title>}} element exists but is empty, causing:

* Browser tabs to show "Untitled" or the URL
* Screen readers to announce no page context
* Confusion for users with multiple tabs open

h3. WCAG Violation

* *WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 2.4.2 (Page Titled) - Level A*
* Every web page must have a descriptive title that describes topic or purpose

h3. Code Location

File: {{/mod/scorm/player.php}} (lines 113-119)

{noformat}if ($displaymode == 'popup') {
    $PAGE->set_pagelayout('embedded');
} else {
    $shortname = format_string($course->shortname, true, array('context' => $coursecontext));
    $pagetitle = strip_tags("$shortname: ".format_string($scorm->name));
    $PAGE->set_title($pagetitle);
    $PAGE->set_heading($course->fullname);
}
{noformat}

h3. Proposed Fix

{noformat}if ($displaymode == 'popup') {
    $PAGE->set_pagelayout('embedded');
    // Add page title for popup mode
    $PAGE->set_title(format_string($scorm->name));
} else {
    $shortname = format_string($course->shortname, true, array('context' => $coursecontext));
    $pagetitle = strip_tags("$shortname: ".format_string($scorm->name));
    $PAGE->set_title($pagetitle);
    $PAGE->set_heading($course->fullname);
}
{noformat}

h2. Issue 2: Missing Title Attribute on SCORM Iframe

h3. Description

The iframe that contains the SCORM content ({{id="scorm_object"}}) is created without a title attribute, making it impossible for screen reader users to understand the purpose of the iframe.

h3. Steps to Reproduce

# Open any SCORM activity
# Inspect the page using browser developer tools
# Find the iframe with {{id="scorm_object"}}
# Observe that it has no {{title}} or {{aria-label}} attribute

h3. Expected Result

The iframe should have a descriptive title attribute.

h3. Actual Result

The iframe lacks a title attribute, causing:

* Screen readers to announce "frame" without context
* Users unable to understand what content is in the iframe
* Difficulty navigating between multiple iframes if present

h3. WCAG Violations

* *WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 2.4.1 (Bypass Blocks) - Level A*
* *WCAG 2.1 Success Criterion 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value) - Level A*
* Frames and iframes must have accessible names

h3. Code Location

File: {{/mod/scorm/module.js}} (lines 93-99 in the {{scorm_activate_item}} function)

{noformat}var obj = document.createElement('iframe');
obj.setAttribute('id', 'scorm_object');
obj.setAttribute('type', 'text/html');
obj.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', 'allowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('webkitallowfullscreen', 'webkitallowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('mozallowfullscreen', 'mozallowfullscreen');
if (!window_name && node.title != null) {
    obj.setAttribute('src', url_prefix + node.title);
}
{noformat}

h3. Proposed Fix

{noformat}var obj = document.createElement('iframe');
obj.setAttribute('id', 'scorm_object');
obj.setAttribute('type', 'text/html');
obj.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', 'allowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('webkitallowfullscreen', 'webkitallowfullscreen');
obj.setAttribute('mozallowfullscreen', 'mozallowfullscreen');
// Add title attribute for accessibility
obj.setAttribute('title', M.util.get_string('scormcontent', 'scorm'));
if (!window_name && node.title != null) {
    obj.setAttribute('src', url_prefix + node.title);
}
{noformat}

h3. Additional Location

The noscript fallback iframe also lacks a title attribute.

File: {{/mod/scorm/player.php}} (lines 228-230)

{noformat}echo html_writer::tag('noscript', html_writer::tag('iframe', '', array('id' => 'main',
    'class' => 'scoframe', 'name' => 'main', 'src' => 'loadSCO.php?id='.$cm->id.$scoidstr.$modestr)));
{noformat}

h3. Proposed Fix for Noscript

{noformat}echo html_writer::tag('noscript', html_writer::tag('iframe', '', array(
    'id' => 'main',
    'class' => 'scoframe',
    'name' => 'main',
    'src' => 'loadSCO.php?id='.$cm->id.$scoidstr.$modestr,
    'title' => get_string('scormcontent', 'scorm')
)));
{noformat}

h2. Language String Addition

Add a new language string to {{/mod/scorm/lang/en/scorm.php}}:

{noformat}$string['scormcontent'] = 'SCORM content';
{noformat}

h2. Testing Instructions

# Apply the fixes
# Test with screen readers (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver)
# Verify page titles appear in browser tabs for popup mode
# Verify screen readers announce iframe purpose
# Run automated accessibility testing tools (axe DevTools, WAVE)

h2. Impact

* *Severity*: High - These are Level A WCAG violations
* *Users affected*: All users relying on screen readers
* *Compliance*: Required for legal accessibility compliance in many jurisdictions

h2. Additional Notes

These issues have been confirmed in Moodle 4.5 but likely exist in earlier versions. Both fixes are minimal code changes that don't affect functionality, only improve accessibility.

This is a follow up to [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85355|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85355|smart-link], because this case was missed there.

Basically, if we don’t have any placement configured for a given tool, and we click “Manage placements” in the course tools tool context menu, we’ll see a funny empty modal. 

There is currently no UX mockup for this case in the prototype, so perhaps a sensible default might be to simply render a warning notification in the form in such cases. E.g.

{noformat}if (empty($statusrecords)) {
    global $OUTPUT;
    // Ignore the hard coded strings here of course...
    $notice = new \core\output\notification('Placements can be configured in the tool\'s configuration.', \core\output\notification::NOTIFY_WARNING, false, 'There are no available placements for this tool', 'i/warning');
    $mform->addElement('html', $OUTPUT->render($notice));
} else {
    // Normal form render stuff..
}{noformat}

And then, once the behat tests have been updated in [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85918|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-85918|smart-link], we can also add/extend a scenario in ltix/tests/behat/managecoursetools.feature covering this case (all we’ll need is a tool without a configured placement and we should see it).
